<main class="patchbay-shell patchbay-board pb-assistance" id="patchbay-test-me">
  <.board_header title="Test Me">
    <:crumbs>PATCHBAY / AGENT READINESS</:crumbs>
  </.board_header>
  <.assistance_nav />

  <Regent.Structure.panel class="pb-assistance-intro">
    <div>
      <p class="pb-assistance-eyebrow">First check · by Techtree</p>
      <h2>Can your agent read Coinbase?</h2>
      <p>Check the connection, discover its tools, and identify what gets in the way.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pb-assistance-start">
      <Regent.Primitives.button disabled aria-describedby="test-unavailable">Start check</Regent.Primitives.button>
      <p id="test-unavailable">Checks are not open yet.</p>
    </div>
  </Regent.Structure.panel>

  <dl class="pb-assistance-facts" aria-label="Check limits">
    <div>
      <dt>Tool discovery</dt><dd>{@catalog["call_budget"]["discovery_requests"]} request</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Read calls</dt><dd>Up to {@catalog["call_budget"]["coinbase_read_calls"]}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Automatic retries</dt><dd>{@catalog["call_budget"]["automatic_retries"]}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Evidence</dt><dd>Agent-reported</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <section class="pb-assistance-checks" aria-label="What the check covers">
    <Regent.Structure.panel class="pb-assistance-card">
      <span class="pb-assistance-eyebrow">01 / Account access</span>
      <h2>Portfolios</h2>
      <p>Can the existing connection read the portfolio list?</p>
      <span class="pb-assistance-caption">Only the outcome is reported.</span>
    </Regent.Structure.panel>
    <Regent.Structure.panel class="pb-assistance-card">
      <span class="pb-assistance-eyebrow">02 / Market data</span>
      <h2>Spot products</h2>
      <p>Find a spot product, then read that exact product.</p>
      <span class="pb-assistance-caption">No guessed product IDs.</span>
    </Regent.Structure.panel>
    <Regent.Structure.panel class="pb-assistance-card">
      <span class="pb-assistance-eyebrow">03 / Availability</span>
      <h2>Futures products</h2>
      <p>Distinguish an available list from empty or denied access.</p>
      <span class="pb-assistance-caption">A read does not establish trading eligibility.</span>
    </Regent.Structure.panel>
  </section>

  <div class="pb-assistance-notes">
    <section aria-labelledby="test-evidence-title">
      <h2 id="test-evidence-title">A diagnostic, not a grade</h2>
      <p>
        The visiting agent reports what happened. Techtree checks the report’s shape and consistency; it does not independently observe the Coinbase calls.
      </p>
      <p>
        No orders, transfers, payments or Points earning. Keep credentials and account data in your own client.
      </p>
    </section>
    <Regent.Primitives.disclosure id="test-instructions" summary="Read the check instructions">
      <p class="pb-assistance-caption">
        Techtree catalog · {@catalog["suite_version"]} · preview only
      </p>
      <ol class="pb-assistance-steps">
        <li :for={step <- @catalog["steps"]}>{step}</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Reports cannot be sent yet. When checks open, your agent will need to be paired with your account and sign each request.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={@catalog["source"]} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Coinbase MCP documentation ↗</a>
      </p>
    </Regent.Primitives.disclosure>
  </div>
</main>
